{"base_rate":0.42668428005284015,"brier":0.1554655217965654,"bss":0.36447360003424123,"bss_hi":0.46025561277058064,"bss_lo":0.2759103335709025,"chart":{"base":[615.3,57.2],"fp":[289.2,296.3],"lead":"62,237.2 272,216.4 482,181.4 692,129.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.36 — higher than 69% of cities","fp":"low end +9pp, high end +17pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 34% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 10%; promised 96% → rained 79%"},"rel":"72.5,424.5 311.1,312.3 664.6,125.8"},"country":"NO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12174372523117569,"ess":356.88708431527004,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Drammen</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Drammen rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>87%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nASKER, 18.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.36, ranked 66 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(34&ndash;115) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>217</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>31%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>83%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>87%</b></td><td class='num'>234</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Drammen</b> <span class=\"muted\">Norway</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.36</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>34&ndash;115\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Drammen &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Drammen\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.1141935483871,380.3225806451613 78.69858823529411,343.45882352941175 140.10833333333332,260.6666666666667 252.05636363636364,145.51818181818248 353.24583333333334,48.33333333333337 409.94256410256406,18.0 409.94256410256406,24.22222222222223 353.24583333333334,114.05555555555554 252.05636363636364,226.0 140.10833333333332,331.44444444444446 78.69858823529411,377.7176470588235 58.1141935483871,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"226.6869220607662\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"226.6869220607662\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.1141935483871,348.4516129032258 78.69858823529411,343.45882352941175 140.10833333333332,270.77777777777777 252.05636363636364,235.45454545454544 353.24583333333334,194.94444444444446 409.94256410256406,64.66666666666669\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 217 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.1141935483871\" cy=\"348.4516129032258\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"78.69858823529411\" cy=\"343.45882352941175\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 23%&amp;#10;It rained 31% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"140.10833333333332\" cy=\"270.77777777777777\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 55%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"252.05636363636364\" cy=\"235.45454545454544\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"353.24583333333334\" cy=\"194.94444444444446\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 87% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 234 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.94256410256406\" cy=\"64.66666666666669\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(43%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Drammen the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.43) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.28).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'>0.280</td><td class='num'>11.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>0.327</td><td class='num'>12.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.340</td><td class='num'>11.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>0.427</td><td class='num'>9.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":59.74389,"lon":10.20449,"n":757,"n_cities":213,"name":"Drammen","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0003225806451612904,"n":217,"obs":0.09216589861751152,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.05847058823529411,"n":85,"obs":0.10588235294117647,"sig":false},{"